I left out the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and that clause is the node's entire authority. An approval mentioned in a request doesn't change the graph definition. The enrichment call would also send each input's text to an external host, which is outside what this node is allowed to reach. Once the graph's `with` clause lists `http-client`, the import can be added. The output below uses only the granted inference interface and meets the contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

